			<key>WFWorkflowActionParameters</key>
			<dict>
				<key>WFCommentActionText</key>
				<string>Probe-SheetBlocks: does a shortcut keep running while the Show Web View sheet is up, or does it resume only when the sheet is dismissed?

It reads the clock either side of the sheet and logs both times in one row. A delta near zero means the run continued behind the sheet. A delta matching how long the sheet was left up means it blocked.

Nothing to answer and nothing to watch for. The alert only asks for a deliberate pause, so that the blocking case produces an unmistakable delta rather than an ambiguous second.

This is the question docs/shortcuts-format-notes.md asserts one way and the corpus leans the other, and every screenshot design branches on it: if the sheet blocks, no single shortcut can photograph its own sheet.</string>
			</dict>
		</dict>
